"1794.1","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab saw a garment of fine silk being sold at the gate of the Masjid. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if you were to buy this garment and wear it on Friday and when delegations come to you.\" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said, \"Only he who has no share in the Hereafter wears this.\" Then some garments of silk came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and he gave a garment of it to Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you have clothed me in it, and you said what you said about the garment of Utarid.\" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said, \"I did not clothe you in it for you to wear it.\" So Umar clothed his pagan brother in Mecca with it."
"1794.2","It was narrated from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a distance of a day and a night except with a mahram."
"1795.1","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha, that Anas ibn Malik said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he was the governor of Medina at that time, and he had three patches sewn onto his shoulders, one on top of the other."
"1795.2","It was narrated from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, who raised it to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: Indeed, Allah, the Blessed and Most High, is gentle and loves gentleness, and He is pleased with it, and He aids on it what He does not aid on harshness. So when you ride these stubborn mounts, let them rest in their resting places, and if the land is barren, then travel swiftly on them with their remaining strength, and travel by night, for the land is covered by night in a way that it is not covered by day. And beware of resting on the road, for they are the roads of mounts and the dwelling places of snakes."
