"1800.2","Malik related to me from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"1801.1","And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Bakr bin Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Umar, from Abdullah bin Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and let him drink with his right hand, for the Shaitan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.\""
"1801.2","Malik narrated that it reached him that a slave girl belonging to Abdullah bin Umar bin Al-Khattab, whom Umar bin Al-Khattab saw, had prepared herself in the manner of free women. So he went to his daughter Hafsah and said: \"Did I not see your brother's slave girl mingling with people, having prepared herself in the manner of free women?\" And Umar disapproved of that."
"1802.1","And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Abu Az-Zinad, from Al-A'raj, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"The miskin is not the one who goes around to people, and a morsel or two, and a date or two, turns him away.\" They said: \"Then what is the miskin, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"The one who does not find enough to suffice him, and people do not notice him so that they give him charity, and he does not stand up and ask people.\""
"1802.2","From Abdullah bin Dinar, that Abdullah bin Umar said: \"When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, to listen and obey, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, would say to us: 'To the best of your ability.'\""
"1803.1","Malik related to me that he heard that Abu Hurayra said that the Messenger of Allah"
"1803.2","Malik related to me that he heard that Abu Hurayra said that the Messenger of Allah"
"1804.1","Malik related to me that he heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab went to the villages every Saturday. If he found a slave doing work which he was not capable of doing"
"1804.2","Malik related to me that he heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab went to the villages every Saturday. If he found a slave doing work which he was not capable of doing"
"1805.1","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a disbelieving guest was hosted by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered a sheep to be milked for him, and he drank its milk. Then another was milked, and he drank its milk. Then another was milked, and he drank its milk, until he drank the milk of seven sheep. The next morning, he became Muslim. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered a sheep to be milked for him, and he drank its milk. Then he ordered another to be milked, but he did not finish it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The believer drinks in one intestine, and the disbeliever drinks in seven intestines.\""
"1805.2","It was narrated from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever says to his brother, 'O disbeliever,' then one of them has returned with it.\""
