"1829.1","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that he heard Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say: A man came to Abdullah ibn Abbas and said to him: \"I have an orphan, and he has camels. May I drink from their milk?\" Ibn Abbas said: \"If you are looking for his lost camels, and tending to their sores, and cleaning their watering troughs, and watering them on their watering days, then drink, without harming the offspring or exhausting the milk.\""
"1829.2","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad used to say: I met people, and they did not marvel at speech."
